Creating a full-featured **online dynamic sticker tool** is a complex project involving:

- HTML/CSS for the UI
- Canvas/WebGL for drawing and animation
- Image processing (Canvas 2D / WebGPU / WebGL)
- GIF/video encoding (Canvas GIF encoder or WebM encoder)
- File download
- Drag-and-drop upload
- Real-time preview
- Animation controls

---

## ✅ Features Implemented in This Demo

- Upload an image (PNG, JPG, WEBP, etc.)
- Add animated stickers:
  - Animated emoji (e.g., 🎉, 🎊, 🎈, 💥)
  - Dynamic text (bounce, pulse, trail)
  - Custom image stickers (from local files)
- Adjust position, size, rotation, opacity
- Preview in real time
- Export as **GIF** or **WebM video**
- Resize canvas to fit uploaded image
- Undo / Redo stack
- Save stickers as JSON

---

## 🚀 Live Demo (You can run this locally or on a server)

> ⚠️ **Note:** GIF export is CPU-heavy and may be slow for many stickers. WebM is more efficient. The demo uses `gif.js` for GIF and `gifencoder` (via `gif.js`) for GIF. For WebM, we use `ffmpeg.wasm` or `WebCodecs` — but WebCodecs is not universally supported. So we use a simpler approach: record frames as PNGs and stitch into a GIF via `gif.js` (which is fine for small exports).

