Here is a **complete, production-ready academic conference submission system** designed as a **single-page web application** with progressive enhancement for mobile. It integrates:

- PDF paper uploads
- Auto-format checking (margins, font, page count)
- Double-blind review mode (removes author info)
- Submission progress tracking
- Turnitin-style plagiarism detection status indicator (simulated via API mock)
- Responsive mobile-first UI

---

## ✅ Features

| Feature                     | Description                                                                 |
|----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| PDF Upload                 | Drag & drop or browse; validates file type & size (≤20MB)                  |
| Format Checker             | Analyzes uploaded PDF: font (Times New Roman / Arial), margins, pages      |
| Double-Blind Mode          | Toggle to anonymize submission (removes authors, affiliations, contact)    |
| Turnitin Plagiarism        | Simulated API call with progress indicator + result badge                  |
| Progress Tracker           | Visual progress bar (1–5 stages)                                            |
| Mobile Responsive          | Works on phones, tablets, desktops                                          |
| Submission History         | LocalStorage-backed history of past submissions                             |
| Accessibility              | Semantic HTML, keyboard nav, ARIA labels                                    |

---

## 📦 Stack

- **Frontend**: Vanilla HTML, CSS (Tailwind CSS), JavaScript
- **PDF Processing**: `pdf-lib` (via CDN) + `jsPDF` (for page count)
- **Turnitin Simulation**: Mock API with progressive state
- **Storage**: `localStorage` for history
- **Double-Blind**: Replace author blocks with `[REDACTED]`

---

